## Cause
`framework/languages/java/zlink-framework-core/src/main/java/systems/zlink/framework/runtime/internal/locations/ZLinkProviderAuthorityRepository.java`:
`readCreationTerminal` (`:736-741`) returns `ZLinkCreationTerminalMissing` unconditionally; `commit` (`:609-675`) takes
the `terminal` argument but writes only authority + capacity; `reject` (`:723-734`) drops the terminal; the abort
variant with a terminal does not persist it either. The in-memory store (`ZLinkInMemoryAuthorityStore.java:541`)
does keep terminals, so tests pass while the provider (Redis) path cannot restore the same OperationId's result —
`ZLinkActorCreationCoordinator.java:353` relies on it. Spec: membership §2 (terminal published together with the
authority/capacity transition; retained until original deadline + 5 min; keyed by source RID + lifecycle generation +
OperationId). Reference: dotnet `ZLinkProviderLocationRepository.Authority.cs:833-924`, node
`location-store-repository.ts:1423-1474` (one conditional write with the terminal put and a TTL).

## What to do
Store the terminal record (envelope + SHA-256 + expiry) in the same conditional write as the authority/capacity
transition for Created, Rejected and Failed; `readCreationTerminal` reads it and validates the identity triple;
recovery-cleanup abort (no terminal argument) stays terminal-free (spec §2 step 7). Regression tests against the
provider repository with a fake provider (replay returns the stored terminal; expiry honored; identity mismatch →
Missing; the two abort variants differ). Kotlin shares the Java path — no separate change expected; say so if true.

